# A digit-string literal beyond even `long`, in Clipping's far-plane float
# slot. GMANRIBTokenize::parseNum's errno check must reject it with
# RIE_RANGE where it is tokenized, before nextFloat ever sees it --
# nextFloat carries no RtInt bound of its own, so a float slot is the only
# place this guard is uniquely observable. An integer slot would let
# nextInt's own new bound catch the tokenizer's saturated LONG_MAX and
# raise RIE_RANGE too, proving nothing about this guard specifically.
#
# A trailing Sphere follows AGENTS.md's "RIB authoring" section, "The
# desync convention."
Display "malformed_out.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 200 200 1
Projection "perspective" "fov" [45]
Clipping 0.5 99999999999999999999
Translate 0 0 5
WorldBegin
Sphere 0.5 -0.5 0.5 360
WorldEnd
